{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:10.7554/eLife.73420","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"35029144","source":"MED","pmid":"35029144","pmcid":"PMC8853656","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC8853656"]},"doi":"10.7554/elife.73420","title":"DunedinPACE, a DNA methylation biomarker of the pace of aging.","authorString":"Belsky DW, Caspi A, Corcoran DL, Sugden K, Poulton R, Arseneault L, Baccarelli A, Chamarti K, Gao X, Hannon E, Harrington HL, Houts R, Kothari M, Kwon D, Mill J, Schwartz J, Vokonas P, Wang C, Williams BS, Moffitt TE.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Belsky DW","lastName":"Belsky","firstName":"Daniel W","initials":"DW","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5463-2212"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Epidemiology & Butler Columbia Aging Center, Columbia University, New York, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Caspi A","lastName":"Caspi","firstName":"Avshalom","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Center for Genomic and Computational Biology, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Corcoran DL","lastName":"Corcoran","firstName":"David L","initials":"DL","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7460-9247"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Center for Genomic and Computational Biology, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Sugden K","lastName":"Sugden","firstName":"Karen","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Poulton R","lastName":"Poulton","firstName":"Richie","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology, University of Otago, Otago, New Zealand."}]}},{"fullName":"Arseneault L","lastName":"Arseneault","firstName":"Louise","initials":"L","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2938-2191"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Social, Genetic, and Developmental Psychiatry Centre, King's College London, London, United Kingdom."}]}},{"fullName":"Baccarelli A","lastName":"Baccarelli","firstName":"Andrea","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Environmental Health Sciences, Columbia University, New York, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Chamarti K","lastName":"Chamarti","firstName":"Kartik","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Gao X","lastName":"Gao","firstName":"Xu","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Occupational and Environmental Health, Peking University, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Hannon E","lastName":"Hannon","firstName":"Eilis","initials":"E","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6840-072X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Complex Disease Epigenetics Group, University of Exeter, Exeter, United Kingdom."}]}},{"fullName":"Harrington HL","lastName":"Harrington","firstName":"Hona Lee","initials":"HL","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Houts R","lastName":"Houts","firstName":"Renate","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Kothari M","lastName":"Kothari","firstName":"Meeraj","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Robert N Butler Columbia Aging Center, Columbia University, Brooklyn, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Kwon D","lastName":"Kwon","firstName":"Dayoon","initials":"D","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7967-8508"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Robert N Butler Columbia Aging Center, Columbia University, New York, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Mill J","lastName":"Mill","firstName":"Jonathan","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1115-3224"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Complex Disease Epigenetics Group, University of Exeter, Exeter, United Kingdom."}]}},{"fullName":"Schwartz J","lastName":"Schwartz","firstName":"Joel","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Environmental Health Sciences, Harvard TH Chan School of Public Health, Harvard University, Boston, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Vokonas P","lastName":"Vokonas","firstName":"Pantel","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medicine, VA Boston Healthcare System, Boston, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang C","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Cuicui","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Environmental Health Sciences, Harvard TH Chan School of Public Health, Harvard University, Boston, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Williams BS","lastName":"Williams","firstName":"Benjamin S","initials":"BS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Moffitt TE","lastName":"Moffitt","firstName":"Terrie E","initials":"TE","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8589-6760"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, Duke University, Durham, United States."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5463-2212"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6840-072X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7460-9247"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7967-8508"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2938-2191"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8589-6760"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1115-3224"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"11","journalIssueId":3287088,"dateOfPublication":"2022 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2022,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Elife","title":"eLife","essn":"2050-084X","issn":"2050-084X","isoabbreviation":"Elife","nlmid":"101579614"},"printPublicationDate":"2022-01-01"},"pubYear":"2022","pageInfo":"e73420","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Measures to quantify changes in the pace of biological aging in response to intervention are needed to evaluate geroprotective interventions for humans. Previously, we showed that quantification of the pace of biological aging from a DNA-methylation blood test was possible (Belsky et al., 2020). Here, we report a next-generation DNA-methylation biomarker of Pace of Aging, DunedinPACE (for Pace of Aging Calculated from the Epigenome).<h4>Methods</h4>We used data from the Dunedin Study 1972-1973 birth cohort tracking within-individual decline in 19 indicators of organ-system integrity across four time points spanning two decades to model Pace of Aging. We distilled this two-decade Pace of Aging into a single-time-point DNA-methylation blood-test using elastic-net regression and a DNA-methylation dataset restricted to exclude probes with low test-retest reliability. We evaluated the resulting measure, named DunedinPACE, in five additional datasets.<h4>Results</h4>DunedinPACE showed high test-retest reliability, was associated with morbidity, disability, and mortality, and indicated faster aging in young adults with childhood adversity. DunedinPACE effect-sizes were similar to GrimAge Clock effect-sizes. In analysis of incident morbidity, disability, and mortality, DunedinPACE and added incremental prediction beyond GrimAge.<h4>Conclusions</h4>DunedinPACE is a novel blood biomarker of the pace of aging for gerontology and geroscience.<h4>Funding</h4>This research was supported by US-National Institute on Aging grants AG032282, AG061378, AG066887, and UK Medical Research Council grant MR/P005918/1.","affiliation":"Department of Epidemiology & Butler Columbia Aging Center, Columbia University, New York, United States.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Economic and Social Research Council","grantId":"ES/S008349/1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"HHSN268201500001C","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NICHD NIH HHS","acronym":"HD","grantId":"R01 HD077482","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"75N92019D00031","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"HHSN268201500001I","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Medical Research Council","acronym":"MRC_","grantId":"MR/N01104X/1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"N01 HC025195","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIA NIH HHS","acronym":"AG","grantId":"R01 AG032282","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIA NIH HHS","acronym":"AG","grantId":"R01 AG066887","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Wellcome Trust","acronym":"WT_","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institute on Aging","grantId":"AG061378","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Medical Research Council","acronym":"MRC_","grantId":"MR/P005918/1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIEHS NIH HHS","acronym":"ES","grantId":"P30 ES009089","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIEHS NIH HHS","acronym":"ES","grantId":"R01 ES025225","orderIn":0},{"agency":"New Zealand Health Research Council","grantId":"16-604","orderIn":0},{"agenc